{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360665-focused-mage-sight-scrutiny-removing-the-extended-action","id":1360665,"title":"Focused Mage Sight - Scrutiny: removing the Extended Action","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-13T03:47:02-08:00","id":1360665,"title":"Focused Mage Sight - Scrutiny: removing the Extended Action","content":"Extended actions really don't work well for my group - it feels too much like rolling dice until a problem goes away, plus the issues with narrating every single roll, plus remembering &quot;so, this is Opacity 4 for player A, player B already brought it down to Opacity 3, Player C still has it as Opacity 7...&quot; is just too much for me.<br /> <br /> So, this is what I'm considering using instead:<br /> <br /> Focused Mage Sight (Scrutiny)<ul><li>Dicepool is Gnosis + Arcana (+1 per Mana spent). The roll is considered a success if it rolls more successes than the Mystery's Opacity (basically, Opacity works like a Withstand).</li> <li>Costs 1 WP (in practice, it's the same WP for keeping up Active Mage Sight up for an extended period of time).</li> <li>Single roll, but the action itself takes a Gnosis Ritual Interval to complete.</li> <li>Each spent Mana gives +1 to the roll. If the roll succeeds, partially recover some of that Mana (up to total spent -1). Succeed or fail, there's a small window in which the Mana can be recovered in other ways (such as Channel Mana).</li> <li>Spending more Mana than your Gnosis is the equivalent of going over the safe number of rolls.</li> <li>Success (rolling more successes than the Mystery's Opacity) gives access to Deep Information (it's the equivalent of reducing Opacity to 0 under the other system).</li> </ul><br /> <br /> I can see some issues with this: we lose out on the ability to dole out partial information (for reducing Opacity for half, for example), and there's no good way to make &quot;slow&quot; progress.<br /> Would you use this system? Any suggestions on improving it, or is there some other obvious flaw I'm missing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T05:47:53-08:00","id":1360679,"title":"","content":"I would say that for your group that may just work. Different groups are going to rule away different things based upon the needs of that group.<br /> <br /> Now, as to what you might miss, I would say locked and linked opacity from Signs of Sorcery. Those two tools give you the ability to truly control your big mystery whereas without them you're mostly just relegated to raising the opacity of the main mystery to absurd levels. Directly related to that is the fact that your case is going to be even more exasperated by that problem since characters HAVE to try to do it in one go.<br /> <br /> Another big issue would be the disparity between acquiring successes vs raising your dicepool. It takes, on average, 3 dice for every 1 success that you want to have a decent shot at. Forcing a Mystery to be done in one go means that some Mysteries could be nigh on impossible to understand since you can only raise your dicepool so high whereas the opacity can be arbitrarily high.<br /> <br /> To give an example of the first issue:<br /> Let's say that your game is set in Los Angelas where the Astral realms are invading normal space. You've got all this cool information about what's going on that you can learn from various different npcs in addition to observing the phenomenon yourself. Because this is a main mystery it's base opacity is probably 5, raised to at least 8 though possibly as high as 10 or 12. Now, in your case that mystery could be (and in fact MUST be) resolved in one single roll. This means that anyone who is lucky could (and in fact MUST) just solve THE mystery that the entire concilium is based upon in a single lucky chance. Where this gets strange (and, unfortunately, poorly done) as related to something like a main mystery as big as the Astral realms invading LA is the sheer number of factors involved with such a Mystery. How could someone possibly just understand everything about something as widespread, convoluted, deep, and involved as an entire REALM invading another with just a single roll? No, this is where locked and linked opacity comes into play. With those two tools you slow it down so that the players are instead forced to understand multiple parts of the Mystery as well as related Mysteries in order to progress with the city wide, BIG Mystery.<br /> <br /> Now, having said that there is a possible compromise: only use the normal system for your main Mystery. This way you can still stretch out that plot without the players just getting it in one go while still allowing for a much simpler system for the rest of the Mysteries that you create. Also, take notes. Yeah, it can be hard to keep track of everything in your head (I wouldn't want to do that either), but if you take notes about where the players are as related to the main mystery then you don't have to worry about each one being at a different stage. Also if you're only doing the normal system for main Mystery and your own for other Mysteries then you have a lot less to keep track of.<br /> <br /> Alternatively you may consider just lowering the opacity a bit for all of your Mysteries. If your intention is for characters to generally be able to understand things in one go then perhaps you just need to lower the opacity.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T06:49:47-08:00","id":1360685,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the feedback. Some specific points I want to address:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360665-focused-mage-sight-scrutiny-removing-the-extended-action?p=1360679#post1360679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, as to what you might miss, I would say locked and linked opacity from Signs of Sorcery. Those two tools give you the ability to truly control your big mystery whereas without them you're mostly just relegated to raising the opacity of the main mystery to absurd levels. Directly related to that is the fact that your case is going to be even more exasperated by that problem since characters HAVE to try to do it in one go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agh, I knew I should have picked up SoS for Christmas. Can you give me a quick and dirty rundown on how that system works?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another big issue would be the disparity between acquiring successes vs raising your dicepool. It takes, on average, 3 dice for every 1 success that you want to have a decent shot at. Forcing a Mystery to be done in one go means that some Mysteries could be nigh on impossible to understand since you can only raise your dicepool so high whereas the opacity can be arbitrarily high. </div> </div> </div>I think the numbers feel right. A Gnosis 1 Apprentice has a decent shot at clearing an Opacity 1 Mystery in one go - but can always spend some Mana to improve his odds - while an Opacity 5 Mystery would be really out of his reach. The fact that a lucky roll can get him there is definitely not an issue here, and a &quot;fluke&quot; can easily be explained within the narrative. Opacity 5 (and higher) <i>should</i> be outside the grasp of unenlightened Mages - if only Masters with decent Gnosis can <i>routinely</i> crack high Opacity Mysteries, we're fine with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To give an example of the first issue:<br /> Let's say that your game is set in Los Angelas where the Astral realms are invading normal space. You've got all this cool information about what's going on that you can learn from various different npcs in addition to observing the phenomenon yourself. Because this is a main mystery it's base opacity is probably 5, raised to at least 8 though possibly as high as 10 or 12. Now, in your case that mystery could be (and in fact MUST be) resolved in one single roll. This means that anyone who is lucky could (and in fact MUST) just solve THE mystery that the entire concilium is based upon in a single lucky chance. Where this gets strange (and, unfortunately, poorly done) as related to something like a main mystery as big as the Astral realms invading LA is the sheer number of factors involved with such a Mystery. How could someone possibly just understand everything about something as widespread, convoluted, deep, and involved as an entire REALM invading another with just a single roll? </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, using the old system means a dedicated enough Disciple can single-handedly solve the story's big Mystery, which... isn't ideal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, this is where locked and linked opacity comes into play. With those two tools you slow it down so that the players are instead forced to understand multiple parts of the Mystery as well as related Mysteries in order to progress with the city wide, BIG Mystery. </div> </div> </div>I really need SoS, huh?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T09:55:40-08:00","id":1360702,"title":"","content":"The only thing I would change is that if you want to treat Opacity like Withstand then don\u2019t require successes to get over it. Treat it exactly like Withstand, letting your players take dice penalties as if they were increasing their Sight\u2019s potency, and then when they roll treat a single success as getting at the deep info. This makes pass/fail less wobbly, and prevents any confusion about how Withstand works for spells when you introduce this house rule to your group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T10:30:59-08:00","id":1360709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360665-focused-mage-sight-scrutiny-removing-the-extended-action?p=1360702#post1360702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing I would change is that if you want to treat Opacity like Withstand then don\u2019t require successes to get over it. Treat it exactly like Withstand, letting your players take dice penalties as if they were increasing their Sight\u2019s potency, and then when they roll treat a single success as getting at the deep info. This makes pass/fail less wobbly, and prevents any confusion about how Withstand works for spells when you introduce this house rule to your group.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... interesting.<br /> <br /> It would mean newly-minted Masters can crack Opacity 5 Mysteries with minimal effort, with ... 16 or 17 Opacity being the absolute top limit that can be understood, which is perfectly acceptable for a Gnosis 10 Master willing to dump tons of Mana into it.<br /> <br /> On the other hand of the spectrum, a Gnosis 1 Apprentice needs to overflood a Mystery with Mana to crack an Opacity 2, and still have pretty good odds of getting an Opacity 1 by themselves.<br /> <br /> Also, this means they get to pick how hard they want to go - if they want the whole thing at once, good for them, but I'd still have the flexibility of being able to consider the Opacity a point or two lower if they were just after some specific information.<br /> <br /> I really like this. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T16:27:57-08:00","id":1360783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360665-focused-mage-sight-scrutiny-removing-the-extended-action?p=1360679#post1360679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, as to what you might miss, I would say locked and linked opacity from Signs of Sorcery. Those two tools give you the ability to truly control your big mystery whereas without them you're mostly just relegated to raising the opacity of the main mystery to absurd levels. Directly related to that is the fact that your case is going to be even more exasperated by that problem since characters HAVE to try to do it in one go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, turns out the bit about locked/linked Opacity were out in the previews. And you're right, those <i>will</i> help. Thanks for the heads-up.<br /> <br /> Okay, rewriting for clarity:<br /> <br /> Focused Mage Sight (Scrutiny)<ul><li>Treat as a Knowing spell, with a +1 bonus to the casting roll per Mana spent, and Withstand equal to Opacity.</li> <li>Costs 1 WP (in practice, it's the same WP for keeping up Active Mage Sight up for an extended period of time).</li> <li>Potency always starts at 1, regardless of Arcana used.</li> <li>No Reach/Yantras can be used on this &quot;spell&quot;.</li> <li>If the roll succeeds, partially recover some of that Mana (up to total spent -1).</li> <li>If you spend more Mana than your Gnosis and the spell fails, increase Opacity by half your Gnosis (round up).</li> <li>Success gives access to Deep Information.</li> </ul><br /> I'm not really good at rules text, but I think this gets the point across.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-14T07:21:50-08:00","id":1360876,"title":"","content":"Things I think needs to be clarified:<br /> <br /> Does the mage/player get to know the Opacity before rolling?<br /> <br /> Does Potency need to be larger than Withstand/Opacity like normal spells, or is it enough to just reduce Withstand/Opacity to 0?<br /> (If the former, the Gnosis 1 Apprentice would need to spend Mana even on Opacity 1 Mysteries to get a more than a 30% shot to succeed.)<br /> <br /> What happens if the mage doesn't have enough Potency but still succeeds at the roll? Do they get partial information instead? Do they still recover most of their spent Mana?<br /> <br /> How are successive attempts handled?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 01-14-2020, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-14T07:37:44-08:00","id":1360878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360665-focused-mage-sight-scrutiny-removing-the-extended-action?p=1360876#post1360876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Things I think needs to be clarified:<br /> <br /> Does the mage/player get to know the Opacity before rolling?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes - rule of thumb, I don't hide mechanical information from my players. If I <i>have</i> to, I give them a Beat in return.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does Potency need to be larger than Withstand/Opacity like normal spells, or is it enough to just reduce Withstand/Opacity to 0?<br /> (If the former, the Gnosis 1 Apprentice would need to spend Mana even on Opacity 1 Mysteries to get a more than a 30% shot to succeed.) </div> </div> </div>Oh. Hmm. Wanted to leave it &quot;like normal spells&quot;, but fair point about the low odds. Don't know if I want to stress the &quot;Mana is important&quot; part, or the &quot;Opacity 1 Mysteries are easy&quot; part. Will have to give this some thought.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What happens if the mage doesn't have enough Potency but still succeeds at the roll? Do they get partial information instead? Do they still recover most of their spent Mana? </div> </div> </div>Partial information, yes. As for the Mana refund... no strong feelings there, so I'd be confortable with anything between &quot;yes&quot; and &quot;yes, but at a reduced rate&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How are successive attempts handled? </div> </div> </div>Same way we handle successive attempts everywhere else - not unless the circunstances change somehow.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-14T08:18:24-08:00","id":1360884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360665-focused-mage-sight-scrutiny-removing-the-extended-action?p=1360878#post1360878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Partial information, yes. As for the Mana refund... no strong feelings there, so I'd be confortable with anything between &quot;yes&quot; and &quot;yes, but at a reduced rate&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spent Mana - ([Opacity] - [Potency] +1) ?<br /> Basically, deduct remaining Opacity+1 from the recovered Mana.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360665-focused-mage-sight-scrutiny-removing-the-extended-action?p=1360878#post1360878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same way we handle successive attempts everywhere else - not unless the circunstances change somehow.</div> </div> </div> </div>The general rule for successive attempts is that you're free to just do it again, only include a cumulative -1 penalty if you're in a pressured situation. Of course, any costs (in this case WP and potentially Mana) would have to be spent again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-14T08:40:17-08:00","id":1360889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360665-focused-mage-sight-scrutiny-removing-the-extended-action?p=1360884#post1360884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spent Mana - ([Opacity] - [Potency] +1) ?<br /> Basically, deduct remaining Opacity+1 from the recovered Mana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems fair.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The general rule for successive attempts is that you're free to just do it again, only include a cumulative -1 penalty if you're in a pressured situation. Of course, any costs (in this case WP and potentially Mana) would have to be spent again. </div> </div> </div>I know, but if there's no pressure at all, we usually just skip the roll altogether. It's one of those houserules we've been using for so long, it feels wrong to do it in any other way <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T09:17:57-08:00","id":1372725,"title":"","content":"After using this for a few sessions, we came to a conclusion: we don't like it. It felt like the best approach to a Mystery is &quot;dump Mana all over it&quot;.<br /> <br /> This is what we're using instead:<ul><li>Dicepool is Gnosis + Arcana (+1 per Mana spent) + progress bonus.</li> <li>Costs 1 WP (in practice, it's the same WP for keeping up Active Mage Sight up for an extended period of time).</li> <li>Single roll, but the action itself takes a Gnosis Ritual Interval to complete.</li> <li>Each spent Mana gives +1 to the roll. If the roll succeeds, partially recover some of that Mana (up to Opacity or successes rolled, whichever's lower).</li> <li>Spending more Mana than your Gnosis is the equivalent of going over the safe number of rolls (after the roll, add half your Gnosis to Opacity, rounded up)</li> <li>Each success peels back one layer of Opacity. Rolling more successes than Opacity fully Scrutinizes it, while rolling under the required number gives only partial information.</li> <li>Failing to fully Scrutinize the Mystery gives a progress bonus. For example, rolling 3 successes on an Opacity 5 Mystery gives you a +3 bonus to further Scrutiny rolls - if on your next roll you get 4 successes instead, the bonus &quot;updates&quot; to +4.</li> </ul><br /> This feels much more variable, and gives us room to experiment with Prime spells to further improve on Scrutiny (granting dice tricks, to bonus dice, to flat-out adding bonus successes).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}